From 32bf745892d158e183853fc7a6a685839a2eccaf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nucleon Dev <dev@localhost>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:22:25 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(client): reveal card phases and remember manual card
 disclosure choices

Hardens the MCP-UI default-visibility patch:

- ActivityPhaseGroup: a settled/folded activity section whose calls carry a
  supported ui_resources attachment is not folded shut, and opens once if the
  card arrives late (same once-only ref rule as ToolCall/ToolCallGroup).
- ToolCallGroup: a card group inside a completed phase is no longer held
  closed by the phase's auto-expand suppression.
- cardDisclosure.ts: module-scoped, in-memory record of the reader's own
  collapse/expand choice (keyed by tool-call id, group/phase by first call id)
  so a remount does not undo it; page-session only, cards only, never written
  by the automatic reveal.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
